{%- comment -%}
  zv-cart-line-group: prints 'huren' or 'kopen' for a cart line (2026-10-28, extracted from
  sections/zv-cart.liquid so /cart and Overzicht cannot decide it differently; see
  docs/cart-huur-koop-split-2026-10-28.md). Capture it, then `| strip`.

  The group is the line's OWN billing cadence, never the flow or toggle that added it (a bought
  Videodeurbel pulls in a monthly camera subscription that is still Huren).
  Huren = recurs monthly (prepaid for the first months today): a rented package (product type),
  Woning, Ontzorgpakket, the camera rider, the two Huren add-ons. Each is recognised by its own
  product (type / the variant-id lists), never by name, SKU text or a quantity guess (a Woning
  line is pkg_qty x its floors, the others pkg_qty).
  Kopen = one-off, quantity 1, never recurs: a bought package (Afname: Kopen, see zv-koop-fk), the
  Koop hardware, the installation lines and, as the default, any plain purchase. The Afname test
  comes first so a Koop product is never swept into Huren.

  Params (render scope can't see the section's variables, so pass them in):
    item                       - the cart line item
    sub_type, sub_tag          - the package product type / tag fallback
    woning_ids                 - woning_variant_id_list
    ontzorg_ids                - zv_ontzorg_variant_id_list
    rider_ids                  - zv_rider_variant_id_list
    addon_videodeurbel_id      - zv_addon_videodeurbel_variant_id (Huren Videodeurbel)
    addon_afstandsbediening_id - zv_addon_afstandsbediening_variant_id (Huren Afstandsbediening)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign zg_vid = item.variant_id | append: ''
  assign zg_group = 'kopen'
  if item.properties['Afname'] == 'Kopen'
    assign zg_group = 'kopen'
  elsif woning_ids contains zg_vid or ontzorg_ids contains zg_vid or rider_ids contains zg_vid
    assign zg_group = 'huren'
  elsif item.variant_id == addon_videodeurbel_id or item.variant_id == addon_afstandsbediening_id
    assign zg_group = 'huren'
  elsif item.product.type == sub_type or item.product.tags contains sub_tag
    assign zg_group = 'huren'
  endif
  echo zg_group
-%}
